<title>SWEDEN: Scania says buys Swiss truck importer.</title>
<headline>Scania says buys Swiss truck importer.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck company Scania said on Friday it had bought a privately-owned Scania importer, Truck AG of Switzerland.  </p>
<p>&quot;The acquistion is estimated to be carried out by May 31,&quot; Scania said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The current owner of Truck AB has decided to divest the operations to Scania ahead of a generation change, which also complements Scania's strategy of integration of sales companies on important markets,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>No financial details were given.</p>
<p>Truck AG, based in Kloten, Switzerland, has been a Scania importer since 1957 and had a turnover of 700 million crowns in 1996, Scania said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
